-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
References consulted during development
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

These projects were read to learn file formats, data layouts and behaviour.
Unless stated otherwise, nothing from them is vendored, linked or shipped, and
no code was copied. Facts learned from them (offsets, layouts, IDs, names) are
documented in docs/ with credit. Policy: docs/licensing.md.

Decompilation and symbols
  dbalatoni13/nfsmw — https://github.com/dbalatoni13/nfsmw — CC0-1.0
    Chunk ID names (tools/bchunk_names.py), struct layouts (TextureInfo,
    eStreamingEntry, TrackStreamingSection, AttribSys classes), PC 1.3 symbol
    map. Read-only reference; behaviour is reimplemented spec-first.
  Brawltendo/Most-Wanted-Vehicles-Decomp — no license — reference only.

Format readers and tools
  NFSTools/NFS-ModTools — https://github.com/NFSTools/NFS-ModTools — no license — reference only
    (solid, scenery and TPK layouts).
  NFSTools/VaultLib — https://github.com/NFSTools/VaultLib — MIT (AttribSys).
  NFSTools/Attribulator — https://github.com/NFSTools/Attribulator — no license — reference only.
  NFSTools/GlobalLib — https://github.com/NFSTools/GlobalLib — MIT (global files, JDLZ).
  NFSTools/FEngLib — https://github.com/NFSTools/FEngLib — no license — reference only (FEng UI).
  SpeedReflect/Nikki — https://github.com/SpeedReflect/Nikki — MIT (strings, collision, sun info).
  SpeedReflect/Binary, NFSTools/Binary — GPL-3.0 — read only.
  vgmstream — https://github.com/vgmstream/vgmstream — ISC-style (EA audio formats).
  FFmpeg (libavformat/electronicarts.c, libavcodec/vp6.c) — LGPL-2.1+ — read only (movie
    container facts: docs/provenance/video.md).
  ruffle-rs/nihav-vp6 — https://github.com/ruffle-rs/nihav-vp6 — MIT (VP6 decoder, used as a
    dependency; see above).
  x07x08/nfsmw-save-editor — https://github.com/x07x08/nfsmw-save-editor — Unlicense (save offsets).
  EA Command & Conquer Generals source, EAC compression library — GPL-3.0 — read for
    understanding the HUFF codec only; see docs/formats/huff.md.

